flowchart TB
    accTitle: A recurring schedule is separate from its queued job and result
    accDescr: A configured enabled interval task is discovered by scheduler_worker, which queues work in Redis. An ordinary queue worker executes it and records a job result. Saving a task alone does not prove execution succeeded.
    subgraph Dispatch["Dispatch due work"]
        direction LR
        A["Configured recurring task<br/>Interval · action · user"] --> B["scheduler_worker<br/>Find due enabled tasks"] --> C["Redis job queue<br/>Waiting work"]
    end
    subgraph Execute["Execute and inspect"]
        direction LR
        D["Ordinary queue worker<br/>start_worker QUEUE"] --> E["Execute the selected action<br/>Check user and operation"] --> F["Inspect job result<br/>Success · failure · logs"]
    end
    Dispatch --> Execute
